.TH SDL_TrayEntryFlags 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_TrayEntryFlags \- Flags that control the creation of system tray entries.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef Uint32 SDL_TrayEntryFlags;
.BI "
.BI "#define SDL_TRAYENTRY_BUTTON      0x00000001u /**< Make the entry a simple button. Required. */
.BI "#define SDL_TRAYENTRY_CHECKBOX    0x00000002u /**< Make the entry a checkbox. Required. */
.BI "#define SDL_TRAYENTRY_SUBMENU     0x00000004u /**< Prepare the entry to have a submenu. Required */
.BI "#define SDL_TRAYENTRY_DISABLED    0x80000000u /**< Make the entry disabled. Optional. */
.BI "#define SDL_TRAYENTRY_CHECKED     0x40000000u /**< Make the entry checked. This is valid only for checkboxes. Optional. */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Some of these flags are required; exactly one of them must be specified at the time a tray entry is created\[char46] Other flags are optional; zero or more of those can be OR\(aqed together with the required flag\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_InsertTrayEntryAt (3)
